**/.classpath
**/.dockerignore
**/.env
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm
**/azds.yaml
**/bin
**/charts
# Safe to leave unanchored because the app is named CodeCoverage, not Coverage.
**/coverage
**/docker-compose*
**/Dockerfile*
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/obj
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
LICENSE
README.md

# Merged from the Coverage repo's own .dockerignore. Only the build-context
# root's file is honoured, so these have to live here rather than beside the app.
**/dist/
**/.angular/
.github/
.playwright-mcp/
docs/
tmp/
# Nx cache. Pure build state, and the Dockerfile runs with --skip-nx-cache anyway.
.nx/
# Test projects. The image never builds or runs them -- the Dockerfile restores and publishes
# CodeCoverage.csproj alone, and no test project is an npm workspace. Measured: they were 714 MB
# of the 742 MB context, almost all of it a leftover tests/MintPlayer.Spark.Tests/bin.stale/ that
# **/bin does not match, because the component is 'bin.stale' and not 'bin'.
tests/
**/*.Tests/
# Root-level only, deliberately: Docker's * does not cross /, so this leaves the
# per-project READMEs and AGENTS.md in the context, which the build is happy with.
*.md
# **/ is load-bearing. `*.pem` alone matches ONLY a root-level key -- it would NOT have
# excluded apps/CodeCoverage/github-app.pem, which is exactly the file this rule exists
# to keep out of an image layer.
**/*.pem

!**/.gitignore
!.git/HEAD
!.git/config
!.git/packed-refs
!.git/refs/heads/**